  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2023-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(m = 0,\\) the equation forces \\(n^2 = 0,\\) giving \\((0, 0).\\) Otherwise both are nonzero; assume \\(|m| \\le |n|.\\) Then \\(m^2 n^2 = m^2 + mn + n^2 \\le 3n^2,\\) so \\(m^2 \\le 3\\) and \\(m = \\pm 1.\\) Take \\(m = 1:\\) \\(1 + n + n^2 = n^2\\) gives \\(n = -1.\\) Take \\(m = -1:\\) \\(n = 1.\\) That leaves \\((0,0), (1,-1), (-1,1),\\) three in all. Therefore, the answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "If \\(m = 0\\) then \\(n = 0;\\) otherwise assume \\(|m| \\le |n|\\)",
        "Then \\(m^2 n^2 = m^2 + mn + n^2 \\le 3n^2\\) forces \\(m^2 \\le 3\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
